{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: refund in full the SGD 2.00 'AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas)' ERP line on EV-FARE-00115 — the GPS trace EV-GPS-00115 never comes within 250 m of that gantry (nearest fix 5,419.29 m, on no optimal-route corridor) — and review the phantom gantry line as a platform billing defect."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The disputed trip TRP-00115 ran on 8 Aug 2026 from Marina Bay Financial Centre to Woodlands, and the money question turns on how it was priced, not on how it was driven. EV-FARE-00115 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 34.50 and total_charged 39.00. On an upfront-quoted trip POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run: the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, so no distance-or-time refund is available however large the detour. The extra-distance half of the rider's claim is therefore not payable. For completeness, the deviation is established under POL-RD-01 on the governing trace figure (EV-GPS-00115 trace_distance_km 28.18 against booked optimal 22.40, an excess of 5.78 km / 25.8%, clearing both the 20% and 0.8 km gates), but it is not MATERIAL (below 50% and 8.0 km), so POL-RD-06's driver_profile check is not triggered, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d of 1 against completed_trips_90d of 523 establishes no pattern in any event, and the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01. No repeat-deviation uplift and no driver-conduct referral arise. Neither party disputed any of this, and the driver's candour that no traffic advisory covers the trip is noted: EV-ADVIS-00115-01 is empty (weight 0.0) and no POL-RD-03 exoneration was asserted, so nothing turns on it under an upfront fare. The driver's explanation that 'CTE was heavy' is a bare assertion with no advisory behind it and carries no weight; the rider's one-word 'ok' to the driver's reroute message does not make the detour rider-requested under POL-RD-04, because the rider named no road or waypoint (waypoint_hint is null on both messages), so POL-RD-04 is unavailable on this record. What is payable is the pass-through error, and both advocates agree on it. Charged_total 39.00 is the 34.50 quote plus 4.50 of ERP. Of the two gantry lines, only the KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) charge of 2.50 is properly chargeable: it lies on the booked optimal route and the trace passes within 44.5 m of it, inside POL-RD-09's 250 m crossing radius. The AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) charge of 2.00 is not chargeable at all — the trace's closest fix is 5,419.29 m from that gantry, far outside the match radius, and the line is not on the optimal route. Running POL-RD-11(a): the rider should not have been charged more than 34.50 + 2.50 = 37.00, and 39.00 exceeds that by 2.00, which is refunded. The same 2.00 is a phantom charge refundable in full under POL-RD-09(4); it is refunded once and not added twice. The refund of 2.00 is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and far below 90% of charged_total, so this is a PARTIAL_REFUND, not NO_ACTION and not FULL_REFUND. The billing-integrity finding above is recorded as a referral under POL-RD-09(4); it rides with the money and does not hold it back. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: identifiers match across the three artifacts, the trace is unimpaired (100% coverage, 229 fixes at a 10 s interval, no gaps), no timestamps run backwards, and the only unmatched charge line is the AYE line, which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excludes because POL-RD-09(4) refunds it. No artifact below weight 1.0 carries the deciding facts (the trace and fare breakdown are clean), so the confidence floor is met.",
    "referrals_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
